  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community-led development and establishment of a Territorial Community Fund to foster social and economic advancement and maximize available resources in small, rural towns located along El Camino de</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community philanthropy in Costa Rica is gaining traction as organizations such as Asociacin Mar a Mar identify opportunities to provide local groups with funding and technical assistance to help them achieve their development goals. At the IAF, we support community-led solutions to unlocking private, public, and community resources for grassroots development. Our grantee partner Mar a Mar works to advance community philanthropy by managing small grants that promote community-led tourism along the Camino de Costa Rica, a hiking trail that extends from the Atlantic to the Pacific Coasts. This grant advances the IAF&apos;s strategic initiative to expand the resources available for grassroots development by promoting locally-rooted community philanthropy.</narrative>
  </description>
